// OrganizationService is the caller's view of the organizations they belong
// to. Users and orgs are many-to-many: a person can be a member of several
// orgs, and an org can have several members (controlplane.org_memberships).
//
// Every org-scoped operation acts in ONE org that the caller is a member of.
// When a request names none, it acts in the caller's DEFAULT org: the one
// SetDefaultOrganization stored, or their oldest membership until they choose.
// There is no "first org of the user" anywhere else. docs/orgs.md is the full
// contract, including how a request names its org.
//
// Callers are HUMANS (a Supabase/Zitadel session). A machine credential
// (an `rlat_` token) is bound to exactly one org when it is minted, so it has
